        "id": 1297255
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-18T20:55:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Patchset7 changed the check condition from \"\u003e\u003dU\" to \"\u003eTIRAMISU\" to be consistent with CTS (aosp/2258806) and thus to fix CTS on AVD.\n\nSpecifically, we have a CTS to require devices with VSR API \u003e TIRAMISU to have this flag enabled. This CTS fails on AVD because AVD\u0027s initial SDK is 34 but value of Android U is now 10000. As the result, the AVD does not have the flag added by SystemConfig but is required by CTS to have this flag.\n\nAnother potential fix is to change the CTS from checking \"\u003eTIRAMISU\" to \"\u003e\u003dU\". However, it does not work because the CTS is part of a mainline module and will automerge to tm-mainline-prod, which means the CTS needs to be built with SDK T where `VERSION_CODES.UPSIDE_DOWN_CAKE`does not exist.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1523,
        "startChar": 71,
        "endLine": 1523,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "c2a39352841f7dc540db0d3dde3050568999af54",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "330d13b8_21a53480",
        "filename": "core/java/com/android/server/SystemConfig.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 1523,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-22T09:25:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are we actually allowed to do this? DEVICE_INITIAL_SDK_INT is the initial device launch version. But given that this feature may require kernel changes / config options, shouldn\u0027t it be set based on the VSR version?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1523,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 1523,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "c2a39352841f7dc540db0d3dde3050568999af54",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ebc6ef7_4ff28b2f",
        "filename": "core/java/com/android/server/SystemConfig.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 1523,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-22T09:26:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "... or is the expectation that any OEM launching a U device with a T-era kernel would fail CTS, then go and change this code?",
      "parentUuid": "330d13b8_21a53480",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1523,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 1523,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "c2a39352841f7dc540db0d3dde3050568999af54",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6ec76da3_d7a45869",
        "filename": "core/java/com/android/server/SystemConfig.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 1523,
      "author": {
        "id": 1297255
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-22T19:39:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e ... or is the expectation that any OEM launching a U device with a T-era kernel would fail CTS, then go and change this code?\n\nYes \n\nIn CTS aosp/2258806 `testHasIpSecTunnelMigrateFeature()`, we only require this feature on devices whose VSR API \u003e\u003d U",
      "parentUuid": "1ebc6ef7_4ff28b2f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1523,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 1523,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "c2a39352841f7dc540db0d3dde3050568999af54",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "575747d8_2d6f4824",
        "filename": "core/java/com/android/server/SystemConfig.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 1523,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-10T03:07:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, but then why can\u0027t we just make things work out of the box on those devices, without the OEM having to change their code? AIUI when a device ships on a vendor frozen kernel, the OEM cannot really change the kernel even if they want to. So it seems better that if the kernel is frozen, the AOSP code just works without the OEM having to change it.\n\nI think we can achieve this by simply making this check the same as the one we see in the CTS test.\n\nThis still won\u0027t prevent OEMs from opting in by setting the flag if they want to.",
      "parentUuid": "6ec76da3_d7a45869",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1523,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 1523,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "c2a39352841f7dc540db0d3dde3050568999af54",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cdee7894_9e0a4b8b",
        "filename": "core/java/com/android/server/SystemConfig.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 1523,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-10T18:42:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We have to consider non-VSR devices for AOSP, and IIRC those device requirements are enforced on INITIAL_SDK_INT.",
      "parentUuid": "575747d8_2d6f4824",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1523,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 1523,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "c2a39352841f7dc540db0d3dde3050568999af54",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4501fab6_879957ff",
        "filename": "core/java/com/android/server/SystemConfig.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 1523,
      "author": {
        "id": 1297255
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-10T21:08:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Like Nathan said, I think the current patch can still encourage non-VSR devices to make the kernel update. Thoughts?",
      "parentUuid": "cdee7894_9e0a4b8b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1523,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 1523,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "c2a39352841f7dc540db0d3dde3050568999af54",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "96cbac95_26381d42",
        "filename": "core/java/com/android/server/SystemConfig.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 1523,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-01-11T00:25:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No objection to encouraging non-VSR devices to do the right thing.\n\nWhat I\u0027m saying here is that for VSR devices running pre-U kernels, we should make this code pass CTS, which means we should not set the flag.\n\nIf we set the flag on those devices, that will just force the OEM to change this code to pass CTS, since the kernel they are using is frozen.\n\nWe\u0027ve that sort of thing several times - see b/254143771, b/258829855 for example. While it\u0027s true that this code isn\u0027t mainline, so it won\u0027t force OEMs to request waivers and force us to rush changes into mainline code like we did for those bugs, what those bugs tell me is that OEMs don\u0027t have the ability to change the kernel. We should not require them to change this code to make their device pass CTS.\n\nIn the event that they can and do want to change the kernel, great - they can always set this flag.",
      "parentUuid": "4501fab6_879957ff",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1523,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 1523,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "c2a39352841f7dc540db0d3dde3050568999af54",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
